        "original_id": "9d2ef83c-ca7e-5be1-80e6-9206c73e7fb8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Carl, Denis \"Snake\" Bélanger, Eric Forrest\n- Organizations: Voivod\n- Products: Bone Against Steel, Negatron\n\nFacts:\n- Max Carl Gronenthal was born on January 29, 1950, and he is an American rock singer, keyboardist, guitarist, and songwriter.\n- Denis \"Snake\" Bélanger was born on August 9, 1964, and he is the vocalist and lyricist of the Canadian heavy metal band Voivod.\n- Voivod singer Denis \"Snake\" Bélanger temporarily left the band in 1994.\n- Bone Against Steel was the last album to feature vocalist and keyboard player Max Carl before the band's 1996 comeback.\n- Negatron was the first Voivod studio album not to feature original singer Denis \"Snake\" Bélanger, with bassist Eric Forrest assuming vocal duties for the recording.",
